From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Reinsmidt <735251+ericreinsmidt@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] The Brick's USB cable speaks NCM rather than ECM, as the GKD
 Pixel 2's does, for Down To The Wire: macOS and Linux have drivers for both,
 Windows only for NCM

---
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/brick_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/brick_defconfig
@@ -211,7 +211,7 @@
 CONFIG_USB_SUNXI_UDC0=y
 CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS=y
 CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_ACM=y
-CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_ECM=y
+CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_NCM=y
 CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_MASS_STORAGE=y
 CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_F_FS=y
 CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_F_MTP=y
